      "title": "Expand Energy Stock Declines 17% YTD: How Should Investors Play It?",
      "summary": "Expand Energy (EXE), the largest U.S. independent natural gas producer formed from the Chesapeake-Southwestern merger, has underperformed its sector by 17.4% YTD despite projected 40.8% earnings growth in 2026. While the company benefits from a discounted valuation, the $1.25B Twin Eagle acquisition, and strong balance sheet improvements, significant headwinds including natural gas price volatility, high capital expenditures ($2.75-2.95B), rising transportation costs, and integration risks warrant a cautious Hold rating.",
